# The published bundle is committed, and CI rebuilds it and fails if the result differs
# from what is checked in. That comparison has to mean the same thing on Windows, where
# this repository is authored with core.autocrlf=true, and on the Linux runner that
# performs the check. Vite emits LF; pinning these to LF everywhere stops a line-ending
# conversion from being mistaken for a stale build.
index.html   text eol=lf
assets/**    text eol=lf
